
Introduction to Spring Framework

Spring Framework is a Java framework used to develop enterprise applications.

It makes Java development:

easy, fast, and loosely coupled

Spring is mainly used for:

Web Applications
Enterprise Applications
REST APIs
Microservices
Daily Life Example

Imagine a restaurant 🍽️

Chef = Business Logic
Waiter = Connection between customer and chef
Customer = User

Spring works like a waiter that connects everything automatically.

Benefits of Spring Framework
1. Loose Coupling

Objects are not tightly dependent on each other.

Daily Example

A TV remote can work with different TVs.

2. Dependency Injection

Spring automatically provides required objects.

Daily Example

Someone gives you a water bottle before you ask for it.

3. Easy Testing

Testing becomes simple.

Daily Example

Checking one part of a machine separately.

4. Lightweight

Uses less memory and resources.

Daily Example

A bicycle is lighter than a truck.

5. Modular

You can use only required modules.

Daily Example

Choosing only the pizza toppings you want 

Spring Architecture

Spring architecture is divided into different modules.

Main Modules
Module	Purpose
Core Container	Manages beans
Spring Context	Provides application context
Spring AOP	Security and logging
Spring JDBC	Database connectivity
Spring MVC	Web application development
Spring ORM	Hibernate integration
Simple Architecture Flow
User → Spring Container → Beans → Application
Types of Containers in Spring
1. BeanFactory
Basic container
Uses lazy loading
Creates beans only when needed
Daily Example

Food is prepared only after a customer places an order.

2. ApplicationContext
Advanced container
Uses eager loading
Creates beans at startup
Daily Example

A school bus is ready before students arrive.

Ways of Dependency Injection
1. Constructor Injection

Dependency is injected through constructor.

Example
public Student(Book book)
Daily Example

A bike comes with the engine already attached.

2. Setter Injection

Dependency is injected using setter method.

Example
setBook(Book book)
Daily Example

Inserting a SIM card into a phone later.

3. Field Injection

Dependency is injected directly into the field.

Example
@Autowired
private Book book;
Daily Example

Putting books directly into a school bag.

Important Point

Main concept of Spring:

IOC (Inversion of Control)

It means object creation and management are handled by the Spring container instead of the programmer.